Fixed all four findings:

- `defaultdict` test now observes per-entry behavior via `put` and no longer claims value storage independence.
- `counter_number` rejects fractional counts; forged-count coverage includes `1.5`.
- `deque_parts`/`stack_cons` validate every spine tree, with malformed-deque push tests.
- The 4,000-item depth test now covers `collections.deque(list)` as well as repeated pushes.

Gates re-run: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (2358 passed, 0 ignored), and `../rbops/verify.sh phase-099` — all pass.
